Revised series have reached the list without an interdiff against
their previous version, though one was asked for in "Re: [PATCH v3]
jails/instances/lab-mail: Initial spec" [1]. "[PATCH v2 0/7] Add just
process-email" [2] and "[PATCH v3 0/6] Add just process-email" [3]
both went out without one. Nothing in the tooling or the skill asked
for it, so it depended on the agent remembering.

Patch 1 makes format-patch.sh refuse -v N for N > 1 unless
--interdiff is given, so a reroll without one fails before it is
formatted. Patch 2 tells the process-email skill to pass --interdiff
and shows how to find the previous version's head from the
Message-ID of its last patch, and states the rule in the mail
workflow guide.

I tested the check with -v 2, -v2, --reroll-count=3, and
--reroll-count 2, each refused without --interdiff and accepted with
it, and -v 1 and no -v accepted as before.

"[PATCH 0/6] Answer the inbox with lab-process-mail" [4] removes this
skill in favor of src/lab-process-mail/prompt.md. Whichever lands
second needs the same Revisions text carried into prompt.md; the
format-patch.sh check holds either way.

